    <!-- ROM tabs screen: help -->
    <string name="rom_help_title">Add games and box art</string>
    <string name="rom_help_adding_header">Adding more games</string>
    <string name="rom_help_adding_body">Copy your games into the folder you chose, including their tracks or discs. Subfolders are included. Pluto checks for changes when you return; Refresh games checks immediately.</string>
    <string name="rom_help_art_header">Box art</string>
    <string name="rom_help_art_body">Artwork is not downloaded automatically. Put a PNG, JPG or WebP image beside the game with the same filename before the extension. For example: Spyro.cue and Spyro.png.</string>
    <!-- Folder and file names (boxart/, covers/, images/, Named_Boxarts/, name-thumb.png) must stay as they are -->
    <string name="rom_help_art_layouts">Pluto also reads the layouts the big front ends write: an image in boxart/, covers/ or images/, RetroArch\'s Named_Boxarts/ set, or a name-thumb.png variant. Then refresh the tab.</string>
    <!-- gamelist.xml is a file name and must stay as it is -->
    <string name="rom_help_gamelist_body">If your folder came from RetroPie, Batocera or another EmulationStation setup that keeps gamelist.xml beside the games, keep it. Pluto reads each entry\'s name and artwork, so games appear with the titles and covers you already curated.</string>
    <string name="rom_help_emulator_header">Emulator setup</string>
    <string name="rom_help_emulator_body">Install the emulator you want, open it once and finish its setup. Some systems need a BIOS file. Pluto opens your games in that app; emulator settings and save files are managed there.</string>

